  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for ImageMagick",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for ImageMagick fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-93586: use-after-free in the `ImagesToBlob` method can lead to a process crash (bsc#1281912).\n- CVE-2026-93587: policy bypass in the PCD, CUBE and HALD coders can lead to extra memory allocation and a denial of\n  service (bsc#1281909).\n- CVE-2026-93588: NULL pointer dereference in the PNM coder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281910).\n- CVE-2026-93589: division-by-zero flaw in the FLIF encoder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281911).\n- CVE-2026-93590: failure to perform policy checks during buffer allocation for image pixels in the UHDR encoder can\n  lead to denial of service (bsc#1281913).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
